    "4.6.1",
    "4.4.2",
    "7.2.1"
  ],
  "description": "The impact test considers the record perspective, every Item named as @producer or in a @distribution of the examined records, and a participant named in none of them. A self-attributed reaffirmation that changes nothing in the record, producer or recipient views, but is the only support a participant outside the minutes' distribution sees, has downstream impact, so its removal is refused naming the expectation. A story's only detection cannot be removed: the story would cease to exist, and the story is listed as the dependent.",
